+# Changes
+
+## Round 0
+
+- Added `parseRanges(text, pageCount)` in `src/parse-ranges.mjs`.
+- Added `tests/parse-ranges.test.mjs`.
+- Documented `parseRanges` in `README.md` beside `paperSize`.
+
+Choices the task left open: spaces around parts and hyphens are ignored; the
+result is sorted and has each page once; empty text, empty parts and backwards
+ranges (`3-1`) throw `RangeError`.
+
+Findings addressed: none (no REVIEW.md yet).
+
+## Round 1
+
+Changed in `src/parse-ranges.mjs`, `tests/parse-ranges.test.mjs` and `README.md`:
+
+- Order is kept as typed (no sorting). Addresses the order finding
+  (`"5,1-3"` gives `[5, 1, 2, 3]`, and so on).
+- Repeats are kept (no de-duplication). Addresses the repeats finding
+  (`"2,2"` gives `[2, 2]`).
+- A backwards range counts down (`"5-3"` gives `[5, 4, 3]`) instead of
+  throwing. Both ends are still checked against 1 to `pageCount`.
+- Open-ended ranges: `"8-"` runs to the last page and `"-3"` runs from the
+  first (`"-1"` gives `[1]`, `"10-"` gives `[10]`).
+- Empty or blank text means every page (`""` with 1 page gives `[1]`).
+- Tests that asserted the opposite (sorting and de-duplication, `"1-"` and
+  `"-3"` refused, empty text refused, `"3-1"` refused) were replaced with tests
+  of the cases quoted in REVIEW.md. README text was changed to match.
+- REVIEW.md checklist items 1-6 were already met; no change needed.
+
+Choices left open: a lone `"-"` and empty parts between commas (`"1,,3"`,
+`"1,"`, `","`) still throw `RangeError`; out-of-range ends of open or backwards
+ranges (`"11-"`, `"-0"`, `"0-"`) throw `RangeError`.
